    "result_text": "All 21 tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`), including the address-normalization checkpoints Cp01, Cp10, Cp11, and Cp12.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented address normalization applied whenever an owner is created.\n\n**`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a canonical normalization that mirrors the existing `setEmail` pattern:\n- `setAddress` now stores the normalized value, so the address is normalized on the way in and returned normalized on the way out.\n- New `static String normalizeAddress(String)` helper: trims, collapses internal whitespace to single spaces, upper-cases, and expands whole-word street-type abbreviations (`ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`) via a small lookup map. Returns `null` for `null` and `\"\"` for whitespace-only input. Token-based expansion avoids clobbering substrings.\n\n**`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 In `addOwner`:\n- Compute `normalizedAddress = Owner.normalizeAddress(...)` and reject with `400 BAD_REQUEST` when it is null/blank (the required-field check now rejects an address that is blank *after* normalization \u2014 `@NotEmpty` alone let whitespace through).\n- Pass the normalized address into both `findHouseholdMembers` (household duplicate detection) and `householdId` (shared household id), so every address comparison uses the normalized form. Stored owner addresses are already normalized via `setAddress`, keeping both sides of the comparison consistent.\n\nThe change is confined to the create path per the spec, and reuses the existing `normalizeForHousehold`/mapper machinery without duplicating logic.",
